  "title": "std::unique_ptr: one owner",
  "chapter": "07-generic-stl",
  "summary": "Slide 179: a unique_ptr owns its object alone. Ownership moves; it is never copied. Deletion is automatic.",
  "code": "struct Order { int id; double price; };\n\nint main() {\n  auto a = std::make_unique<Order>( 1, 100.5 );\n  std::unique_ptr<Order> b;\n  // auto c = a;          // error: copy is deleted\n  b = std::move( a );     // ownership moves\n  b.reset();              // delete now\n  auto c = std::make_unique<Order>( 2, 99.0 );\n}                         // c deletes its Order",
